{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_20a009df664e61bfc1fab5883ffdaf18122e1848d14ec0abaa395fba87551768"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Compared with Claude Code, the plugin lacks diagnostic sharing and instead uses the IDE's built-in LSP, per the feature comparison table."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3075399ab082c7bf0b56a04e51bdb7292c2d46f40005f688c06628dc6a181232"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Keyboard shortcuts are customizable through the IDE's Settings > Keymap by searching for 'OpenCode'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3f8a08c6c2bf80b33696ce9d6ee8f5cc936cc76ee8c3a6c7911200cdbee7d649"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An 'Add to Terminal' shortcut (Opt+Cmd+K / Ctrl+Alt+K) sends the current file or selection to OpenCode as @path references, with line ranges like @file.kt#L10-25 when text is selected, and opens/focuses the terminal if needed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4c659e5453f2d3bbf804db99fc5e3cc597b2d7d75d3579033a43e1191c39c1c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin sends a system notification when OpenCode transitions from Busy to Idle, and supports auto-resume of the last session, clickable file-path links in terminal output, and remembered connection settings."},{"claim_ids":["clm_62693995a7cda1947e2628d6322e9d29d62a2fd097dd264e7f5aa536d05048d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Quick Launch opens a connection dialog via Cmd+Esc (Mac) or Ctrl+\\ (Win/Linux), letting users connect to an existing OpenCode server by host:port with optional password, or create a new local terminal session on default port 127.0.0.1:4096."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7037ef48717412d06df0a7a43f0a6103b330152c719e5d2a8550456da26ab406"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Terminal management uses a single persistent terminal tab per project named OpenCode({port}); closing it causes a new one to be created on next launch."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e25e208166cb5dc1c1319bb78f939e0b82e4298ecd02a0c2f57ad46d0ee3b04"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a JetBrains IDE plugin integrating the OpenCode open-source AI coding agent into the development workflow."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8b77dd19e5dbbd1cc3e1e0c6058b9ece3d09ceaa9a63f1c8425b1d560dd292b8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Context can also be added via right-click menus: 'OpenCode: Add Context' in the editor and 'OpenCode: Add File(s)' in Project View."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ade1e4a868f9f75f1ffa85e288b4c11297093fd1c566e3535decb2adb7786985"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin appears to detect server authentication automatically when connecting to a running OpenCode server, and supports an optional password for the server."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca7bf6032a54297a3670afef99f389a443ce764586ea39df64827f3bd98b5513"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plugin requires a JetBrains IDE (2025.2+ per README) and the OpenCode CLI, installable via npm or from opencode.ai/download."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3ad5b1ba6459ba94d125443ccb4d2e6f9c6cba715b54d2978591cc01da43113"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"When OpenCode edits files, the plugin opens a native IDE diff viewer showing changes chronologically with navigation, progress count, and accept (write to disk and git add) or reject (restore pre-edit state) actions."}],"claim_ids":["clm_20a009df664e61bfc1fab5883ffdaf18122e1848d14ec0abaa395fba87551768","clm_3075399ab082c7bf0b56a04e51bdb7292c2d46f40005f688c06628dc6a181232","clm_3f8a08c6c2bf80b33696ce9d6ee8f5cc936cc76ee8c3a6c7911200cdbee7d649","clm_4c659e5453f2d3bbf804db99fc5e3cc597b2d7d75d3579033a43e1191c39c1c2","clm_62693995a7cda1947e2628d6322e9d29d62a2fd097dd264e7f5aa536d05048d4","clm_7037ef48717412d06df0a7a43f0a6103b330152c719e5d2a8550456da26ab406","clm_7e25e208166cb5dc1c1319bb78f939e0b82e4298ecd02a0c2f57ad46d0ee3b04","clm_8b77dd19e5dbbd1cc3e1e0c6058b9ece3d09ceaa9a63f1c8425b1d560dd292b8","clm_ade1e4a868f9f75f1ffa85e288b4c11297093fd1c566e3535decb2adb7786985","clm_ca7bf6032a54297a3670afef99f389a443ce764586ea39df64827f3bd98b5513","clm_f3ad5b1ba6459ba94d125443ccb4d2e6f9c6cba715b54d2978591cc01da43113"],"crea